Tone: premium, educational, confident. Never use the word \"transformation\" lazily. Avoid before-and-after thirst-trap clichés. Use natural contractions. No em dashes. We are positioning ourselves as the smartest, most credible option in our market.`));

// --- Prompt 6 ---
children.push(h3("Prompt 6: Front Desk Objection Handler"));

children.push(para("Use case: real-time training tool for your front desk and consultants. When a patient pushes back on price, this prompt generates a confident, on-brand response in under 10 seconds."));

children.push(promptBlock("Prompt", `You are coaching the front desk team at [SPA NAME] in real time. A patient just objected to a package or membership price. The objection is: [PASTE EXACT OBJECTION].

Generate three response options the consultant can use immediately:

Option 1: Restate the value. Walk through the stand-alone value of every component in the package and remind the patient what they're actually getting. Keep it under 60 seconds spoken.

Option 2: Offer the payment plan or alternative entry point. Klarna or Affirm financing for the full package, or the lowest-tier on-ramp (Gut Reset Starter at $897, or Glow Member at $197/month). Keep it under 45 seconds spoken.

Option 3: The graceful exit. If the patient is clearly not the right fit, give the consultant a script that closes the conversation warmly without discounting, leaving the door open for a future return. Keep it under 30 seconds spoken.

Critical rules:
- Never discount the package price. We don't break pricing.
- Never sound desperate. We're confident in the value.
- Always preserve the patient relationship. Even a no today is a yes in 6 months if we handle it well.
- Use natural contractions, like a real human in conversation.
