children.push(para("Where the membership relationship is actually built. The patient came back. They got blood drawn. They are now sitting in front of you waiting to find out what's wrong with them. Treat this with the gravity it deserves."));

children.push(h3("Setup"));
children.push(bullet("Print the labs, don't just show a screen. The physical paper signals seriousness."));
children.push(bullet("Highlight in advance the three to five values that matter most for this patient. You're a curator, not a reader."));
children.push(bullet("Have the recommended protocol drafted before they walk in. Don't workshop it live."));

children.push(h3("Open with the headline"));
children.push(para("\"Before we walk through everything, here's the headline. [One sentence summarizing what the labs reveal about the patient's primary complaint.] Now let me show you why I'm saying that.\""));
children.push(para("This is the inversion. Most providers walk through every value top to bottom. The patient is anxious by minute three and tunes out. Lead with the conclusion, then back into the data."));

children.push(h3("Walk three to five markers, not twenty"));
children.push(bullet("Pick the markers that explain the patient's symptoms."));
children.push(bullet("For each: \"This is what it is. This is where it should be. This is what it means for how you feel.\""));
children.push(bullet("Skip the markers that are normal. Don't bury the signal."));

children.push(h3("Present the protocol"));
children.push(bullet("Frame it as cause and effect. \"Because your X is doing Y, we want to do Z.\""));
children.push(bullet("Match the protocol to a membership tier. Show what's included, what it costs à la carte, and what the membership saves."));
children.push(bullet("The patient should leave understanding what's happening in their body and what's happening on their schedule for the next 90 days."));

children.push(h3("Close"));
children.push(para("\"I want to see you back in 30 days for the first follow-up. The membership at this tier covers everything we just talked about. Should we get you started today?\""));

// Consult 3: Membership Conversion
children.push(h2("Framework 3: The 20-Minute Membership Conversion"));
children.push(para("For the patient who has done two or three packages with you and hasn't enrolled yet. They're warm. They like you. They just haven't been asked the right way."));

children.push(h3("The script"));
children.push(bullet("\"I want to talk to you about something I've been thinking about for you specifically.\""));
children.push(bullet("\"You've done [X package] and [Y package] with us, and what I'm noticing is the work we're doing with you fits a pattern. Patients who get the result you're looking for usually need [list 3 services] consistently for at least 6 months.\""));
children.push(bullet("\"Right now you're paying à la carte every time. If you keep going at this pace, you'll spend [calculate the realistic à la carte cost] this year. The membership at the level that fits you covers all of that for [member rate], and it includes [the upgrades they don't currently get].\""));
children.push(bullet("\"I'd rather see you on the membership, because honestly, the patients on it get better outcomes. The protocol is consistent. We're not stopping and starting. Does that make sense for where you are right now?\""));

children.push(h3("If they say not yet"));
children.push(bullet("\"What would have to be true for it to be a yes in three months?\""));
children.push(bullet("Document the answer. Calendar a check-in for that exact time horizon."));
children.push(bullet("Don't push. The patient who says yes under pressure churns in 60 days. The patient who says yes at the right time stays for years."));

children.push(pageBreak());

// ===== PART FOUR: AI PROMPTS =============================================

children.push(sectionLabel("Part four"));
children.push(h1("AI prompts you can deploy this week"));

children.push(para("Every prompt below is designed to be copied, lightly customized to your clinic and patient base, and pasted into ChatGPT, Claude, or whatever AI tool you already use. Replace the bracketed placeholders with your specifics. Don't post AI output without reviewing it. Use it as the rough draft, then add the voice."));

children.push(callout([
  { t: "Rule of thumb: AI is fastest at the first 70%. Your team's job is the last 30%. The 30% is where the brand voice lives, and that's what patients actually feel.", italics: true, color: NAVY },
]));

children.push(spacer(160));

// Prompt 1
children.push(h2("Prompt library"));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 1: Membership pitch email",
  "After a patient completes a package and is ready to be invited into a membership.",
  `You are writing a warm, personal email to a medspa patient on behalf of [CLINIC NAME].

Patient context:
- Patient name: [NAME]
- Recent service: [PACKAGE COMPLETED]
- Stated goal in their last consult: [PATIENT GOAL]
- Membership being recommended: [MEMBERSHIP TIER]
- What's included in that membership: [LIST 4-5 ITEMS]
- Member rate: [PRICE]

Write a 200-word email that:
1. Opens with a specific reference to their last visit, not a generic greeting
2. Connects what we noticed during that visit to why this membership fits them specifically
3. Lists what's included in clear, benefit-led language (not feature dumps)
4. States the member rate and the equivalent à la carte value
5. Ends with one clear call to action: book a 15-minute call to enroll

Voice: warm but not casual. Confident. No emojis. No exclamation points. Use natural full sentences, not corporate phrasing. Never use em dashes; use commas, colons, or rewrite the sentence.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 2: Discovery consult prep brief",
  "The morning of a consult. Generate a one-page brief for the provider based on intake data.",
  `You are preparing a 1-page consult brief for a medspa wellness provider.

Patient intake info:
- Name and age: [NAME, AGE]
- Stated primary concern: [WHAT THEY WROTE ON INTAKE]
- Secondary concerns: [LIST]
- Existing medications and supplements: [LIST]
- Past procedures: [LIST]
- What they've tried that didn't work: [LIST]

Generate:
1. Three likely root-cause hypotheses to explore in conversation (hormones, gut, inflammation, metabolic, mitochondrial, skin barrier, sleep, stress).
2. The 4 specific discovery questions the provider should ask first.
3. Two membership tiers and one package most likely to fit, based on the intake.
4. Two red flags to listen for that would change the recommendation.

Format as a clean one-page brief the provider can read in 3 minutes. Use bullet points only where they help comprehension.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 3: Lab result patient summary",
  "After labs are run. Generates the patient-facing language explaining what their results mean. Provider reviews and edits before sending.",
  `You are writing a patient-facing summary of recent wellness labs for a medspa client.

Patient: [NAME]
Key markers and values:
- [MARKER 1]: [VALUE] (reference range: [RANGE])
- [MARKER 2]: [VALUE] (reference range: [RANGE])
- [MARKER 3]: [VALUE] (reference range: [RANGE])
[continue for all markers reviewed]

Patient's stated symptoms or goals: [LIST]

Write a 300-word summary that:
1. Opens with the headline finding (the most important thing this patient should know)
2. Explains 3-5 markers in plain language, connecting each to how the patient feels day to day
3. Notes which markers are in optimal range (not just "normal lab range") and which need work
4. Previews the protocol the provider will recommend, without prescribing
5. Closes by inviting them to the lab review consult to walk through it together

Voice: clear, warm, intelligent. Treat the patient like the smart adult they are. No jargon without translation. Never use em dashes.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 4: Stacked offer rewrite",
  "Take an existing service or package and reframe it as a stacked offer with hero outcome and value math.",
  `You are rewriting a medspa service description as a stacked grand-slam offer.

Current service: [CURRENT NAME AND DESCRIPTION]
What's actually included if you list everything: [LIST EVERY COMPONENT, INCLUDING THINGS PATIENTS DON'T USUALLY THINK OF: CONSULT TIME, FOLLOW-UP, TAKE-HOME ITEMS, ACCESS, RESCHEDULING POLICIES]
Hero outcome the patient is buying: [ONE SENTENCE]
Current price: [PRICE]
À la carte value of everything included: [DOLLAR VALUE]

Rewrite this as a package offer that:
1. Names the package after the outcome, not the procedure
2. Lists every included component as a benefit, with stacked value
3. Quotes the total value and the package price side by side
4. Includes a one-line positioning statement explaining why this exists and who it's for

Format: package title, one-line subtitle, bulleted inclusion list with values, total stacked value, package price, one-line positioning. No discounts. No urgency tactics. No exclamation points. No em dashes.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 5: Patient nurture sequence (4-email cold lead reactivation)",
  "For patients who haven't booked in 90+ days. Drops them back into the funnel without sounding like a sales blast.",
  `Write a 4-email reactivation sequence for medspa patients who haven't booked a service in 90 or more days.

Clinic context: [CLINIC NAME], focus on [WELLNESS / GLOW / PERFORMANCE / RESET].
Hero membership being introduced in this sequence: [MEMBERSHIP TIER + WHAT IT INCLUDES].
Patient persona: women and men 35-60, aesthetically aware, increasingly interested in longevity and wellness.

Sequence structure:
- Email 1 (Day 1): Re-introduction. Acknowledge it's been a minute. Share what's new in the practice. No ask.
- Email 2 (Day 4): Educational. Pick one health topic (gut, hormones, sleep, peptides, GLP-1, glow from the inside) and write a short, useful piece on it. Soft CTA to a free 15-minute discovery call.
- Email 3 (Day 8): Patient story. A composite example (no real names, no real photos) of a patient who came in with [PROBLEM] and what their 90 days looked like. Soft CTA to the Longevity Diagnostic package.
- Email 4 (Day 12): Direct offer. Introduce the membership. Stacked value, member rate, clear CTA to book the consult.

Each email: 180-250 words. First-person from the practice owner or wellness lead. Warm but not salesy. No em dashes, no emojis, minimal exclamation points.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 6: Front desk script for inbound peptide and GLP-1 inquiries",
  "Standardize how the front desk handles the increasing volume of patients calling about peptides and weight loss meds.",
  `You are writing a front desk inbound call script for [CLINIC NAME] for patients asking about GLP-1s, peptides, or longevity protocols.

Common patient questions:
- "Do you do Ozempic / semaglutide / tirzepatide?"
- "How much is it?"
- "Can I just get a prescription?"

Write a script that:
1. Validates the patient's interest without rushing into pricing
2. Pivots from "do you have it" to "let's understand what's going to actually work for you"
3. Books them into the discovery consult, not directly into a prescription
4. Briefly previews what the discovery consult includes and the consult fee (credited toward any package or membership)
5. Handles 3 common objections: "I just want the prescription," "Can you just tell me the cost?", "I've already done labs somewhere else"

Voice: confident, warm, never salesy. Front desk should sound like a knowledgeable concierge, not a receptionist. Length: a one-page script the staff can practice in 10 minutes. No em dashes.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 7: Social media caption pack for a longevity service launch",
  "Generate the caption library when you launch a new membership or package.",
  `Generate a social media caption pack for [CLINIC NAME] launching the [MEMBERSHIP OR PACKAGE NAME].

Hero outcome: [WHAT THE PATIENT GETS]
Who it's for: [PATIENT PERSONA]
What's included: [LIST]
Price: [PRICE]

Generate:
1. One Instagram feed caption (180 words). Story-led, opens with a question or scene the patient recognizes themselves in. CTA: "DM us LONGEVITY for the full breakdown."
2. Three Instagram story slide captions (one sentence each). Designed to be paired with branded graphics.
3. One short-form video script (45 seconds, conversational, first-person from the practice owner or wellness lead).
4. One LinkedIn post (250 words) for the practice owner's personal profile, professional voice, focused on the why behind launching this service.
5. Three TikTok hooks (one sentence each) that could open a longer video.

Voice: confident, warm, intelligent. Patient is treated as a smart adult. No clickbait. No fake urgency. No em dashes. Minimal exclamation points. Never use the words "girlies," "bestie," or any lowercase trend phrasing.`
));

children.push(...promptBlock(
  "Prompt 8: Internal team training brief",
  "Train the staff on a new offering before it goes live. Use this when adding peptides, IVs, GLP-1, or any new wellness protocol.",
  `Generate an internal training brief for [CLINIC NAME] staff on a new service: [SERVICE NAME].

Service overview: [WHAT IT IS]
What it does for the patient: [BENEFIT]
Who it's right for: [IDEAL PATIENT]
Who it's NOT for: [CONTRAINDICATIONS, IDEAL EXCLUSIONS]
Pricing structure: [À LA CARTE, PACKAGE, MEMBERSHIP]
Common patient questions: [LIST]

Generate a one-page brief that includes:
1. The 30-second pitch every team member can deliver
2. Top 5 patient questions and the staff answers
3. The three most common objections and how to handle each
4. How this service fits with our existing memberships and packages (cross-sell map)
5. What red flags would prompt a staff member to route the patient to the prescriber or owner before booking

Format: clean, scannable, designed to be reviewed in a 15-minute team huddle. No em dashes.`
));

children.push(pageBreak());

// ===== PART FIVE: HOW TO DEPLOY ==========================================

children.push(sectionLabel("Part five"));
children.push(h1("How to deploy this in your clinic"));

children.push(para("Don't roll out everything in this playbook at once. The clinics that win are the ones that pick a focus, install it cleanly, and measure for 90 days before adding the next layer."));

children.push(h3("The 90-day rollout"));

children.push(bulletMixed("Days 1–30: pick one package and one membership. ", "Run them. Train your team on the consult framework. Track conversion from consult to package, package to membership."));
children.push(bulletMixed("Days 31–60: add one second package. ", "Cross-sell to your active patient base. Measure attach rate."));
children.push(bulletMixed("Days 61–90: introduce the membership conversion script. ", "Run it on every patient who has completed two or more packages. Measure conversion."));

children.push(h3("The metrics that matter"));

children.push(bullet("Consult-to-package conversion rate. Target: 60% or higher within 90 days."));
children.push(bullet("Package-to-membership conversion rate. Target: 35% or higher."));
children.push(bullet("Average member tenure in months. Target: 9+ months by quarter two."));
children.push(bullet("Average revenue per active patient (ARPP) per month. Target: meaningful upward trajectory month over month."));

children.push(h3("What to do when something doesn't work"));

children.push(para("If a package isn't selling, the answer is almost never the price. It's the offer. Rework the stacking, rename the package after the outcome instead of the procedure, and re-pitch it. If a membership isn't converting, look at where the patient hesitated in the consult, not at the price tag."));

children.push(callout([
  { t: "If you'd rather not run this build alone, that's why Luxora exists.", bold: true, color: NAVY, size: 24 },
  { t: "We install all of the above (memberships, packages, consult frameworks, AI systems, and the staff training that makes them stick) inside our 90-Day Growth Engine. If you're reading this and thinking \"I want this in my clinic by next quarter,\" that's the conversation to have.", color: "333333" },
  { t: "go.theluxoracollective.co/the-luxora-growth-engine", color: GOLD, italics: true },
]));

children.push(spacer(200));
children.push(para("Build it well, build it once, and let the patient stay for years.", { italics: true, color: GREY, before: 200 }));
children.push(para("Bethany Anne & Eric", { bold: true, before: 200 }));
children.push(para("The Luxora Collective", { color: GREY, before: 0 }));
children.push(para("theluxoracollective.co", { color: GREY, italics: true, before: 0 }));

// ----- Document assembly -------------------------------------------------

const doc = new Document({
  creator: "The Luxora Collective",
  title: "The Longevity Stack Playbook",
  description: "Memberships, packages, consults, and AI prompts for medspa owners",
  styles: {
    default: { document: { run: { font: "Calibri", size: 22 } } },
  },
  numbering: {
    config: [
      {
        reference: "bullets",
        levels: [{
          level: 0,
          format: LevelFormat.BULLET,
